{
  "AC": "",
  "ActualSummary": "Single-version schema migrator. One SCHEMA_VERSION now spans the sqlite table shape and the record JSON shape; record migrations are an ordered RECORD_MIGRATIONS registry applied by migrate_record (which stamps _schema), with the legacy field-renames folded in as the v6 step that normalize_todo_schema delegates to. New migrate-to-latest CLI sweeps every record in either backend, writes back changed ones, and advances a per-store data_version marker (distinct from the table schema_version); a cheap startup check warns interactive users when behind. Frozen end-to-end oracle (now live) + 8 new unit tests; full suite 201 green.",
  "BaseSha": "0f4421743bce7a7bcba89d4f1de8b829d8d4679d",
