    "raw": "A separate binary / module -- `migrate-to-latest` -- that owns todo-storage\nschema versioning and migration across BOTH storage backends (sqlite db and\nper-todo JSON files).\n\nWhat it does:\n- Understands both storage backends (db and file) and reads/writes each.\n- Scans and loads ALL todos, updating every record to the NEWEST schema.\n- Each schema carries a meta var recording the current schema version (stored\n  with the data). migrate-to-latest compares stored version vs the code's\n  latest to decide: up-to-date, or migration needed.\n- A quick up-to-date check runs on EACH startup (cheap: compare version meta);\n  the full migrating scan runs only when behind.\n- Must be kept up to date: every schema change adds a migration step here.\n\nWhy: schema migration today is ad-hoc and scattered -- normalize_todo_schema\ndoes inline field renames on every read (Chunks->WorkItems, Subtickets->\nSubtodos, Parent dict->list, Scope path strip). There is no stored schema\nversion and no single migrator. As the record shape evolves -- e.g. ee1799aa\nturns the flat `Tags` string list into a plural embedded `Tag` element list --\na real versioned migrator is needed.\n\nScope / touch points:\n- New module + entry point (`migrate-to-latest`, or a todo.py subcommand\n  fronting it).\n- A schema-version meta field on stored records (and/or a store-level version).\n- An ordered migration-step registry (vN -> vN+1) applied to reach latest.\n- Startup hook: cheap version check; migrate (or warn) when behind.\n- Fold in / supersede the ad-hoc normalize_todo_schema migrations.\n- Backends: todo_store (file dir) and sqlite (todo_db).\n\nRelationship: motivated by and unblocks the ee1799aa flat-`Tags` -> plural\n`Tag` migration, but is broader than tags -- it owns all schema evolution.\n\nWorking model (Opus orchestrator / Sonnet implementor): worked per\nskills/projectmanagement/PLAN.md -- the model-assignment doc for AC-gated\nWorkItems. Each WorkItem AC is a frozen test; a Sonnet subagent codes to green,\nand Opus (this model) authors the ACs, verifies the diff, and integrates."
  },
