      "sha": "3cfa607d82e117a0af488fb1eb6e8feb2811550a",
      "summary": "END TEST (skip until impl): migrate-to-latest brings a below-latest store (legacy Chunks/singular-Parent records; stored version < SCHEMA_VERSION) to latest across BOTH sqlite and file-dir backends; every record and the stored version == SCHEMA_VERSION; a second run is a no-op"
    },
    {
      "done": true,
      "kind": "code",
      "message": "test(todo_db): cover RECORD_MIGRATIONS ordering and data_version round-trip\n\nRecordMigrationRegistryTest verifies migrations apply ascending and skip\nversions at/below the record's current _schema, and that a version with no\nregistered transform is a harmless no-op. MigrateRecordTest exercises the\nreal v6 transform through migrate_record and its idempotence.\nDataVersionMarkerTest round-trips get/set_data_version on both backends and\nconfirms it stays independent of the sqlite schema_version table.",
      "sha": "7767b1d963fc234df2c8e867fd4e5be91d9e1345",
      "summary": "Unified migration registry keyed by version: each step has an optional table-DDL and an optional record-transform (record->record); migrate_record applies transforms in version order, no-op steps skip cleanly, idempotent, latest record unchanged; UNIT TEST"
    },
